          "path": "_m/k/s/f/3/victoria-falls-zimbabwe-wp/national-railways-zimb.jpg",
          "filename": "0855 VictoriaFallsZimbabwe 19920803.jpg",
          "caption": "National Railways of Zimbabwe 15A class 4-6-4+4-6-4 'Garratt' locomotive no. 407 'Ukhozi' ('Eagle', built by Beyer Peacock in 1950) has been positioned for photographic purposes with a short train on Victoria Falls bridge for a couple of hours.\n\nA small fee bought a pass to walk onto the bridge, which can be seen to also have a road and a footpath.  Victoria Falls town in Zimbabwe is behind the train which is facing towards Zambia, the Zambezi River is below, and Victoria Falls is away to the right.  There was a steady stream of vehicles and pedestrians across the bridge, and a few trains (when this train was not there!).",
          "alt": "National Railways of Zimbabwe 15A class 4-6-4+4-6-4 'Garratt' locomotive no. 407 'Ukhozi' ('Eagle', built by Beyer Peacock in 1950) has been positioned for photographic purposes with a short train on Victoria Falls bridge for a couple of hours.\n\nA small fee bought a pass to walk onto the bridge, which can be seen to also have a road and a footpath.  Victoria Falls town in Zimbabwe is behind the train which is facing towards Zambia, the Zambezi River is below, and Victoria Falls is away to the right.  There was a steady stream of vehicles and pedestrians across the bridge, and a few trains (when this train was not there!).",
